# Gagauz single-language site

Shared, tool-agnostic copy also lives in **`AGENTS.md`** at the repo root; update both when norms change.

- **Audience language**: The site has no language switcher and no parallel locales. All **user-visible** text (navigation, headings, buttons, labels, footers, error messages shown to visitors, `<title>`, `meta description`, Open Graph text) must be **Gagauz**.
- **Document language**: Root HTML must declare Gagauz, e.g. `<html lang="gag">`. Use **UTF-8** everywhere (`charset="utf-8"`, UTF-8 encoded files) so Gagauz letters and punctuation render correctly.
- **Stories**: Body text of stories, legends, and tales is **Gagauz** only. Do not add English/Romanian/Russian “summary” blocks unless the user explicitly asks.
- **Avoid i18n sprawl**: Do not introduce `en.json` / `ro.json` style locale files or translation keys for this project unless the user explicitly requests multilingual support.
- **Developer text**: Code comments, internal variable names, and git commit messages may remain in English for tooling and collaboration unless the user prefers otherwise.

```html
<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
<html lang="gag">

<!-- ❌ BAD for this repo -->
<html lang="en">
```
